              <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{t}\leftarrow E^{\prime}\cup E_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{t}\leftarrow E^{\prime}\cup E_{new}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{t}=(V,E^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{t}=(V,E^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>. </span><span id="S6.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">HyperLLM Fits Real-World Hypergraphs.<span id="S6.T2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Comparison of HyperLLM against baselines on fitting structural patterns across 8 datasets. The question mark (?) indicates that size distribution is not strictly required; for small-scale datasets, our model can achieve high-fidelity generation even without this input, showcasing its flexibility. The <span id="S6.T2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">best</span>, <span id="S6.T2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">second-best</span>, and <span id="S6.T2.8.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#DAA520;">third-best</span> average rankings are highlighted.</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="S6.T2.9" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T2.9.1" class="ltx_tr">
